load @term/call/work/home
  find root, name project-root

load @term/call/work/small/version-move
  find call-move

# `term move mark [1|2|3|rc]` -- bump the package version, or start or move a pre-release named by a word (`code`
# is the target's old spelling).
#
# The hook binds `bump-code`, so the verb is that task. It takes the hook's arguments and hands them to the handler,
# the small lane's port of deck/call/code/move.ts (work/small/version-move.tree `call-move`), which rewrites the
# manifest and prints through the output library. It prints nothing of its own, catches nothing and never exits: a
# throw reaches dispatch.tree `fail-line` (decision 005 of cli-in-term, part 2).

# line.ts passed `argv.target` and `argv.level`, absent when not named, and callMove names an absent target `that` in
# its refusal where an empty one names nothing. The hook hands an absent argument over as the empty text, so the
# empty text is none here
task given
  take value, like text

  like maybe, like text

  fork test, is-equal(value, <>)
    hold
      back make none
  back make(some, value)

task bump-code
  mark async
  take target, like text
  take level, like text

  like void

  # the project root is READ, not taken: a hook has no `root` argument to pass
  save root, call project-root
  call-move(root, given(target), given(level))
